    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0762" n="677" xml:id="pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2610</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bluefields</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sanders</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July
                        25.</hi>]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 291</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>As for the expulsion decree incident, however, I am glad to report that I
                    consider the matter closed; …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>… the decree was shortly ordered suspended. According to my private information,
                    it was so ordered on June the 25th. The Governor of Bluefields got the news
                    officially on the 28th. …</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John O. Sanders</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
